    {
      "type": "posts",
      "id": "270782",
      "links": {
        "self": "/posts/270782"
      },
      "attributes": {
        "number": 1,
        "createdAt": "2026-11-25T20:49:49+00:00",
        "contentType": "comment",
        "contentHtml": "<h3>The issue</h3>\n\n<p>So I've been running Flarum for the last four years since migrating over from MyBB.  It worked mostly ok up until a couple of days ago, when users started reporting things breaking - quote button disappearing, reply to button disappearing, notifications stopping working, tags were not displaying, users could post threads without tags, etc. I noticed it happening to me first in Brave and then in Chrome, yet it still worked in Firefox.</p>\n\n<p>I decided to upgrade today, hoping that might solve the issues. It was at 1.6, so I upgraded to 1.8, and then to 2.0. The issues remained plus a whole heap more, so I tried deleting the install and doing a fresh install, and then reconfigured it to point to the existing database. I've just about got it back to working to the level it was at before (except I had to delete all my plugins and customisations in the upgrade), but the major issues from pre-upgrade remain (no tags, can post without tags, no reply/quote buttons, no text options on the quick reply window, no post reporting), plus now the website doesn't work at all for me in Firefox (I can only get the header bar) and I can't access the admin panel in Chrome (I get the navigation bar, but the main window is empty).</p>\n\n<p>Any suggestions would be appreciated, because I'm at a bit of a loss here. My forum is onemoreinthetolly.com/forums/</p>\n\n\n<h3>Flarum information</h3>\n\n<p>I'm on 2.0, MariaDB 11.4.13, php 8.3.</p>",
        "renderFailed": null,
        "source": null,
        "sourceName": null,
        "editedAt": "2026-11-25T20:57:49+00:00",
